-- Q4508: Materiality [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): AU-C 320.12 requires the auditor to revise materiality if information obtained during the audit would have caused a different amount initially. A significant revenue decrease from $10 million to $7 million warrants downward revision and reassessment of whether planned audit procedures remain sufficient.
Wrong (A): Maintaining the original level ignores the auditor''s obligation to revise materiality when circumstances change during the audit.
Wrong (B): A 30% revenue decline is not a normal fluctuation that can be ignored—it materially changes the benchmark underlying the materiality calculation.
Wrong (D): Increasing materiality for a smaller entity contradicts the principle that lower benchmarks generally require lower materiality thresholds.$EXPL$
