  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): When using net income before taxes as a benchmark, auditors commonly apply 5% to 10%. This range is widely accepted in practice per AU-C 320.A7 guidance, though the specific percentage depends on professional judgment and the entity''s circumstances.
Wrong (A): A 1% to 2% range is too low for net income before taxes and would result in an impractically small materiality amount for most entities.
