-- Q4514: Materiality [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per AU-C 450.A18, materiality is not solely quantitative. A misstatement that is quantitatively immaterial may be qualitatively material if it triggers a debt covenant violation, changes a loss to a profit, or involves fraud. The auditor must evaluate both quantitative and qualitative factors when assessing materiality.
Wrong (A): Ignoring the misstatement based solely on its dollar amount overlooks qualitative factors that AU-C 450 requires the auditor to consider.
Wrong (C): Adjusting materiality upward to make a misstatement immaterial is inappropriate and would undermine the integrity of the materiality determination.
Wrong (D): A covenant violation has implications for users beyond management; it must be considered for the audit report, not merely communicated to management.$EXPL$
