-- Q4517: Materiality [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per AU-C 450.11, when aggregate uncorrected misstatements ($160,000) exceed performance materiality ($150,000), the auditor should be concerned that total uncorrected and undetected misstatements could exceed overall materiality ($200,000). Additional procedures, management corrections, or opinion modification may be necessary.
Wrong (B): Exceeding performance materiality is specifically designed to trigger action before overall materiality is breached—the auditor cannot simply wait.
Wrong (C): Being below overall materiality does not mean the statements are fairly presented when performance materiality has been exceeded and undetected misstatements may exist.
Wrong (D): Increasing performance materiality to accommodate known misstatements defeats its purpose as a safety margin and violates AU-C 320.$EXPL$
